# Terraform-generated state and lock files.
#
# `terraform.tfstate` contains all provisioned resource IDs *and may
# contain plaintext secrets* (Hetzner returns the SSH key, R2 access info
# is computed, etc). Never commit. State lives on the operator's Mac for
# the first apply; migrate to remote state in R2 once the bucket exists
# (see runbooks/first-deploy.md).
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# *.tfvars holds the real values for sensitive variables. The shape goes
# in terraform.tfvars.example, the values stay local.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Plugin downloads + per-init scratch space — large and reproducible.
.terraform/

# `.terraform.lock.hcl` records exact provider versions resolved at last
# init. Committing it (recommended) means everyone running `terraform
# init` gets the same provider binaries. NOT gitignored.

# Crash dumps if a provider panics.
crash.log
crash.*.log
